applies to bone files as well. Is it frowned upon to keep backups of 
generated bone files? I'm not talking about that lucky (Unlucky?) time 
when your near ascension character just got done putting his stuff in a 
bag of holding after being poisoned by some bad food seven turns after 
his spell of cure sickness expired. No, I mean the bones of characters 
that couldn't have ascended if they managed to find a blessed wand of 
wishing (0:999). Especially when you completely pass them by and the 
bone file is deleted without you ever even running into them.

I just like my dungeon littered with the corpses of ne'er'do'wells; 
